00:37:10.230 --> 00:37:10.490
Then?

00:37:11.950 --> 00:37:12.950
That's where I wake up.

00:37:14.840 --> 00:37:15.880
Standing by the doors.

00:37:17.270 --> 00:37:18.390
Planes coming in low.

00:37:19.420 --> 00:37:20.220
Bombs dropping.

00:37:21.340 --> 00:37:21.800
Strafing.

00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:24.080
That's just where I wake up.

00:37:27.740 --> 00:37:29.120
Realistic and very frightening.

00:37:31.530 --> 00:37:32.730
How long has this been going on?

00:37:33.520 --> 00:37:34.700
How often have you had this dream?

00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:36.400
Every night for a week.

00:37:37.190 --> 00:37:38.330
Everything is always the same.

00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:40.340
Chronologically the same.

00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:40.760
Everything.

00:37:41.240 --> 00:37:41.580
Everything.

00:37:42.980 --> 00:37:44.180
The ensign and his bride.

00:37:45.270 --> 00:37:45.850
The bar.

00:37:46.890 --> 00:37:48.090
In my room on the phone.

00:37:48.230 --> 00:37:48.450
Everything.

00:37:50.310 --> 00:37:56.360
And the moment when I'm standing by those doors and the planes are coming in, it's always the same.

00:37:59.490 --> 00:37:59.970
And it's...

00:38:02.200 --> 00:38:06.640
It's real. It's not a dream. It's real. I'm going back in time.

00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:17.280
Mr. Jensen, I won't attempt to analyze that dream now except to say this,

00:38:17.340 --> 00:38:20.060
that very often you dream with a purpose.

00:38:21.570 --> 00:38:25.420
Dreams are usually significant to something deep-rooted in a man's subconscious.

00:38:26.840 --> 00:38:29.980
Very often the subjects that you dream about are not really the thing.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:38.050
that bother you. They're only symbols of the things that bother you. Look, Doc, don't try to

00:38:38.050 --> 00:38:46.550
out logic me. I'm not trying to pass this off as logic. I just know what I know. I'm going back in

00:38:46.550 --> 00:38:53.440
time. I can't give you an explanation. I thought maybe you could give me one. And I'll tell you

00:38:53.440 --> 00:38:59.760
something else. When I'm standing by those doors and the planes are coming in, that's where I wake up.

00:39:00.960 --> 00:39:04.000
But even after I wake up and I'm lying in bed thinking about it,

00:39:05.280 --> 00:39:06.960
I know the dream shouldn't have ended there.

00:39:08.180 --> 00:39:09.680
It should have gone on beyond that.

00:39:12.080 --> 00:39:13.980
One of these nights it will go on beyond that.

00:39:15.580 --> 00:39:18.820
And you have no idea what might transpire in that moment beyond that?

00:39:19.250 --> 00:39:19.470
No.

00:39:33.200 --> 00:39:35.040
All right, let's approach it your way.

00:39:36.710 --> 00:39:39.650
Let's look at it as if it weren't a dream, but let's look at it very practically.

00:39:41.780 --> 00:39:44.300
Assume now that it were possible to go back in time.

00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:45.460
Now we can assume that.

00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:49.950
You go back in time and you do something.

00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:54.680
Let's say you warn people about an accident that you know is going to happen

00:39:54.680 --> 00:39:56.040
so that the accident doesn't happen.

00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:59.040
But what is it that you're doing?

00:40:01.148 --> 00:40:02.488
by altering the past.

00:40:03.420 --> 00:40:04.440
You change the present.

00:40:06.492 --> 00:40:07.152
Look, Doc...

00:40:07.152 --> 00:40:09.112
Now, this is important, Mr. Jensen, it's...

00:40:09.148 --> 00:40:10.748
Very important that you grasp this.

00:40:12.924 --> 00:40:13.944
Let's try this analogy.

00:40:16.188 --> 00:40:17.188
Supposing...

00:40:18.204 --> 00:40:19.844
supposing I were able to go back in time.

00:40:21.436 --> 00:40:22.676
Now go back and...

00:40:22.780 --> 00:40:23.180
I'm hit.

00:40:23.484 --> 00:40:24.664
Well, let's say by a taxi.

00:40:26.140 --> 00:40:29.640
Now it figures that if I were able to go back in time and were killed,

00:40:30.348 --> 00:40:31.388
I wouldn't be living today.

00:40:32.236 --> 00:40:32.936
Not only that,

00:40:33.804 --> 00:40:35.264
Think of all the other lives affected.

00:40:36.716 --> 00:40:37.556
Wouldn't have gotten married.

00:40:37.636 --> 00:40:38.336
Wouldn't have any children.

00:40:38.764 --> 00:40:39.724
I wouldn't have bought a house.

00:40:40.812 --> 00:40:43.312
All these things wouldn't exist as they do today.

00:40:43.884 --> 00:40:46.404
because I changed them in the past by being killed.

00:40:47.884 --> 00:40:48.104
Ciao.

00:40:48.524 --> 00:40:48.804
So.

00:40:49.740 --> 00:40:51.480
It's not possible to go back in time.

00:40:52.268 --> 00:40:54.268
We must assume that this is a dream.

00:40:57.804 --> 00:40:58.964
All right, try this then.

00:40:59.564 --> 00:40:59.884
All right?

00:41:06.204 --> 00:41:10.024
I've never been in Honolulu in my whole life before, except during that dream.

00:41:12.540 --> 00:41:15.420
So, after the first couple of times I dreamed this, I...

00:41:19.004 --> 00:41:19.504
Take your time.

00:41:22.620 --> 00:41:24.560
Well, I decided I'd put it to a test.

00:41:26.204 --> 00:41:28.264
I knew the ensign's last name. It was an odd one.

00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:28.880
Janoski.

00:41:30.668 --> 00:41:33.848
He told me that he and his girl had come from a little town called White Oak, Wisconsin.

00:41:34.892 --> 00:41:36.012
I placed a call there.

00:41:36.940 --> 00:41:38.440
There was only one Janoski in the book.

00:41:38.500 --> 00:41:39.560
A woman answered the phone.

00:41:40.428 --> 00:41:41.588
She told me she was his mother.

00:41:43.020 --> 00:41:45.480
I told her that I was an old friend of his from Honolulu.

00:41:47.084 --> 00:41:49.084
I asked was he there?

00:41:50.572 --> 00:41:52.572
and then

00:41:55.596 --> 00:41:59.976
And then she told me that her son and his wife were killed in Honolulu on December 7th.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:00.700
1941.

00:42:02.364 --> 00:42:03.784
He went down with the Arizona.

00:42:03.944 --> 00:42:06.764
She was shot down near King Street by a plane strafing.

00:42:11.644 --> 00:42:13.644
doctor.

00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:18.520
Are you sure you've never been to Honolulu?

00:42:19.644 --> 00:42:20.824
Yes, I was there once.

00:42:21.628 --> 00:42:22.628
When?

00:42:23.484 --> 00:42:25.264
when I'm supposedly having that dream.

00:42:34.412 --> 00:42:35.512
All right, Doc, tell me.

00:42:40.972 --> 00:42:41.972
I don't hear you talking.

00:42:46.252 --> 00:42:46.752
Well...

00:42:50.764 --> 00:42:51.604
at the moment.

00:42:52.044 --> 00:42:53.264
I don't quite know what to say.

00:43:13.116 --> 00:43:16.156
Dr. Gillespie's patient lay on the couch almost in a stupor.

00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:18.016
They've been talking for hours.

00:43:18.716 --> 00:43:19.416
It was Saturday.

00:43:19.740 --> 00:43:22.580
and Gillespie had planned to close early and go play golf.

00:43:23.420 --> 00:43:25.260
At that moment, he'd forgotten golf.

00:43:26.236 --> 00:43:29.796
He was concerned only with the fascinating and unbelievable story.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.640
this man in front of him had told him.

00:43:32.492 --> 00:43:33.012
And then,

00:43:33.548 --> 00:43:35.388
As he looked at him lying there on the couch,

00:43:35.708 --> 00:43:38.128
Dr. Gillespie knew Jensen was falling asleep.

00:43:38.988 --> 00:43:41.928
He could tell by the look on the face that he was far from resting.

00:43:42.476 --> 00:43:45.496
though his eyes were closed and he was no longer aware of him.

00:44:31.820 --> 00:44:32.120
Thank you.

00:45:01.050 --> 00:45:02.610
Wait a minute, repeat.

00:45:03.130 --> 00:45:04.490
He may not be alive tomorrow.

00:45:05.270 --> 00:45:09.860
I told you I don't want no trouble, you hear me?

00:45:16.230 --> 00:45:19.100
Jensen, Jensen.

00:48:27.200 --> 00:48:29.970
this analogy Mr. Jensen, supposing I

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:36.060
were to go back in time and I were to be hit, say, by a taxi. Now it figures if I went back

00:48:36.060 --> 00:48:39.120
in time and were killed, I shouldn't be living today.

00:49:04.960 --> 00:49:05.480
Yes, sir?

00:49:05.830 --> 00:49:06.670
Bourbon on the rocks.

00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:27.360
Bourbon on the rocks.

00:49:28.630 --> 00:49:29.030
Well...

00:49:30.090 --> 00:49:30.570
Happy dreams.

00:49:30.980 --> 00:49:31.700
Whatever you like.

00:49:32.290 --> 00:49:32.730
Drake Hardy.

00:49:48.710 --> 00:49:49.090
Nothing wrong?

00:49:50.970 --> 00:49:51.410
No.

00:49:53.610 --> 00:49:54.490
Who's the guy in the picture?

00:49:56.420 --> 00:49:56.640
Him?

00:49:57.060 --> 00:49:58.200
No, the other picture.

00:49:59.360 --> 00:49:59.900
Well, that's Pete.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.560
Jensen. He used to tend by here.

00:50:02.440 --> 00:50:02.600
No.

00:50:04.670 --> 00:50:05.030
Jensen?

00:50:05.150 --> 00:50:09.860
Just look familiar, that's all.

00:50:13.060 --> 00:50:13.640
Where is he now?

00:50:14.980 --> 00:50:16.380
Dead. He was killed at Pearl Harbor.

00:50:16.850 --> 00:50:29.970
It is October 4th, 19...

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.740
1858, Saturday, 12.10 p.m.

00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:37.390
If anyone is remotely interested in the element of time.

00:50:46.660 --> 00:50:50.380
You're watching an all-night sneak preview of Nick at Night's TV Land,

00:50:50.730 --> 00:50:52.530
the new 24-hour network.

00:50:52.950 --> 00:50:55.730
If you like what you see, call your cable company

00:50:55.730 --> 00:50:58.090
and tell them to add this channel to your service.
